         <div type="bio">
            <p>Parisian bookseller, publisher, editor, and poet. She opened her bookshop, “Maison des amis des livres”, in 1915; it became a magnet for contemporary French writers such as Claudel, <name type="person" key="larb81">Larbaud</name>, <name type="person" key="farg76">Fargue</name>, <name type="person" key="gide69">Gide</name>, and Valery. Monnier encouraged <name type="person" key="beac87">Sylvia Beach</name> to open a bookshop in 1919, which led to her acquaintance with JJ. Her literary review, <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">Le Navire d’argent</name>, published JJ’s “From Work in Progress” (2, no. 5 [1 October 1925], 59-74). Monnier was the organizer and eventually publisher of the French translation of <name type="work" key="W_ULYSSES">Ulysses</name>, appearing first as fragments in <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">Commerce</name> (1, i [Summer 1924], 121-58), and then as the entire <name type="work" key="W_ULYSSES">Ulysse</name> (Paris: La Maison des Amis des Livres, Adrienne Monnier, 1929). She sided with Sylvia Beach in the rupture with JJ in the early 1930s. Following a period of serious illness, Monnier committed suicide in 1955. <hi rend="bold">William Brockman</hi>
                </p>
         </div>
